   This is  a b s o l u t e  nonsense.  If Andy, or anyone else, can
   show how the Branch Davidians could have resisted the BATF goons
   in such a way as to "incapacitate" them without killing them,
   please enlighten the rest of us.  I'm not talking surrender.
   Just tell us some of the many ways you would have stopped the
   attackers without using lethal force (i.e., force that has a
   significant likelihood of causing serious injury or death).

I mean PLENTY in terms of possibilities,  although I realize that
there aren't very many realistic alternatives to guns at this point.
That to me is tragic,  because a large portion of fatal shootings
occur within households.  And around half of all police officers
killed by guns are killed with their OWN guns.  It would be difficult
to kill an police officer with their own gun in England,  since they
don't carry them.

- chemicals (mace, tear gas, etc)
- tranquilizer darts
- tasers
- low-frequency sound waves
- things that haven't been invented yet

I understand that it is relatively impractical now,  but I think
there could be a market for weapons that don't kill but stop an
attacker just as quickly as a gun.  Using chemicals is easier
than using guns because you don't have to be a good aim.

If enough people value human life to believe that it isn't
necessary to kill at the slightest provocation,  then an industry
will develop around non-lethal self-defense,  assuming that the
frequency and magnitude of violence in our society continues to 
increase.

Also, I'm sure the government has developed some things along
these lines in classified research projects.

   I'm reminded of when I moved to San Francisco.  I lived with a
   group of libertarian types in the Haight where we published a
   magazine.  The house was overrun with mice.  The editor didn't
   want us to kill them; she wanted a nice, non-lethal solution
   instead.  I told her to call a hardware store and see what they
   had to offer.  She called and asked if they had any mouse traps
   that didn't kill the mice.  The guy at the store was silent for a
   few seconds, and then replied, "Well, they don't kill them ALL
   the time."  After that, in secret, the rest of us set traps and
   killed mice (but not ALL the time).  It wasn't fun and it wasn't
   pretty, but it was the only thing that WORKED.

